import json,re,sys
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(sys.argv[1]);data={}
CASES={
 'clear-path':('Storm giant: open path','The original carries a blocked-projectile decision over to the giant\'s area spells. It stays and loses 54 HP. The per-spell correction uses one Phase Door scroll and moves behind a wall, retaining 130 HP in this recording.'),
 'blocked':('Storm giant: mold in the path; still-hit counterexample','A visible yellow mold lies between the giant and Rogue. Area spells can still reach the Rogue. The correction spends a scroll, but the destination remains exposed: it still loses 54 HP. The original loses 59 HP without spending a scroll.'),
 'ball-control':('Control: patriarch area spell','The patriarch has an area spell without an earlier boulder. Its original and per-spell-corrected choices and native results are unchanged.'),
 'direct-control':('Control: orc shaman direct attack','The orc shaman\'s direct wounding attack precedes its projectile. Its original and per-spell-corrected choices and native results are unchanged.'),
 'boulder-control':('Control: hill giant; separate path defect remains','The primary per-spell correction leaves the hill giant case unchanged: the separate path helper still counts the caster itself as blocking its own boulder. The path-only and combined diagnostic change that behavior and are separate from the proposed source patch.')}
for mode,(label,explanation) in CASES.items():
 item={'label':label,'explanation':explanation}
 for phase in ('before','path-only','both','after'):
  raw=(root/f'{phase}-{mode}.log').read_text();frames=[json.loads(l[6:]) for l in raw.splitlines() if l.startswith('FRAME ')]
  assert len(frames)==3
  match=re.search(r'OUTCOME (.*)',raw);outcome={k:int(v) for k,v in re.findall(r'(\w+)=(-?\d+)',match[1])}
  danger=int(re.search(r'DANGER current=(\d+)',raw)[1])
  assert frames[0]['hp']-frames[2]['hp']==outcome['hp_lost']
  assert frames[0]['scrolls']-frames[2]['scrolls']==outcome['scrolls_spent']
  item[phase]={'frames':frames,'outcome':outcome,'danger':danger,'raw':raw}
 data[mode]=item
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>The giant's area spell is not its boulder</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#f4f1ea;color:#253a3c;font:18px/1.6 system-ui}main{max-width:1100px;margin:auto;padding:32px 24px}h1{font-size:42px;line-height:1.2}h2{font-size:24px}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.card{background:white;border:1px solid #cbd6d0;border-radius:12px;padding:24px;margin:18px 0}.cards .card{border-top:6px solid #648e80}.hp{font-size:40px;font-weight:750}select,button{font:inherit;max-width:100%;padding:10px;border:1px solid #aabdb5;border-radius:7px;background:white}button{cursor:pointer;margin:14px 8px 0 0}button.active{background:#24685d;color:white}.summary{background:#e6eee6;padding:20px;border-left:5px solid #377367}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font:13px/1.5 monospace;max-height:330px;overflow:auto}details{background:white;padding:20px;margin:20px 0}summary{font-weight:700;cursor:pointer}@media(max-width:650px){.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:32px}}</style><main><p>Recorded native threat estimate, escape choice and scheduled native spell</p><h1>A blocked boulder makes the Borg dismiss the giant's area attacks</h1><p>The Borg treats a storm giant's boulder as unable to reach it, then carries that decision over to the giant's lightning area attacks. In the open-path recording it stays and loses 54 HP. After the per-spell correction it uses one Phase Door scroll, moves behind a wall and keeps all 130 HP.</p><p>The mold-in-the-path example shows the limit: the correction spends a scroll but lands in another exposed square and still takes 54 HP. This is not guaranteed escape or uniform safety. A separate defect also makes the caster count as blocking its own projectile; both corrections are tested independently below.</p><section class="card"><label for="scenario">Choose a recorded situation</label><br><select id="scenario"></select><p id="explanation"></p><label for="variant">Compare the original with:</label><br><select id="variant"><option value="after">Proposed fix: assess each spell separately</option><option value="path-only">Alternative: only correct the projectile path</option><option value="both">Diagnostic: both corrections together</option></select><br><button data-step="0">Start</button><button data-step="1">Show escape choice</button><button data-step="2">Show scheduled spell</button></section><div class="cards"><section id="original" class="card"><h2>Original</h2><div class="hp"></div><p class="stats"></p><p class="action"></p></section><section id="compared" class="card"><h2 id="variant-title"></h2><div class="hp"></div><p class="stats"></p><p class="action"></p></section></div><p class="summary" id="outcome"></p><h2>What the alternatives establish</h2><p>Correcting the projectile path alone changes the open-path example, but leaves the mold-blocked mixed attack underestimated: the Rogue still stays and takes 59 HP. Assessing each spell separately restores the area-attack estimate in both cases. The independent boulder-path problem remains outside the proposed patch; the hill giant control exposes it.</p><details><summary>Experiment conditions and limits</summary><p>Native Human Rogue level 20, 130 HP, depth 38, seed 1000, known Phase Door spell and one scroll, constructed Intelligence/arena setup. The actual stock monster spell lists retain their normal order. One scheduled spell belongs to the actual caster: storm giant/patriarch ball of lightning, orc shaman wounding, hill giant boulder. The native active-monster context supplies the caster's real spell power.</p><p>Production danger/escape code chooses. Exact spell/book or scroll keys are validated and executed natively. Afterward one native spell effect is scheduled only if the actual caster still has range and a terrain-clear path. This selects a valid attack for the experiment; it does not run monster AI spell selection, casting failure frequency, a full player fallback turn or a whole fight. Native damage, saving throws, item use and movement are not substituted.</p><p>Different actions naturally consume different random draws; seed/setup are unchanged and RNG is not reset between decisions. The native Phase Door spell has a 5% failure chance in this setup; shown attempts succeed. A danger estimate is a heuristic, not predicted HP damage. No encounter-frequency or death claim.</p></details><details><summary>Recorded native output</summary><h3>Original</h3><pre id="original-log"></pre><h3>Compared</h3><pre id="compared-log"></pre></details><p>Canonical report: <a href="https://github.com/diegoami/neo-angband-tracker/issues/64">issue64 / CBUG-0048</a>. Discovery credit for mixed-spell finding: borg-rs. Independent caster-blocking defect found by the clear-path control.</p></main><script>
const data=__DATA__;let step=2;const select=document.getElementById('scenario'),variant=document.getElementById('variant');for(const [key,c] of Object.entries(data)){let o=document.createElement('option');o.value=key;o.textContent=c.label;select.append(o)}function draw(){let c=data[select.value];document.getElementById('explanation').textContent=c.explanation;document.getElementById('variant-title').textContent=variant.options[variant.selectedIndex].text;for(const [panel,phase] of [['original','before'],['compared',variant.value]]){let d=c[phase],f=d.frames[step],p=document.getElementById(panel);p.querySelector('.hp').textContent=`${f.hp} / ${f.max_hp} HP`;p.querySelector('.stats').textContent=`Mana: ${f.mana}. Phase Door scrolls: ${f.scrolls}. Position: (${f.x}, ${f.y}). Borg danger estimate: ${d.danger}.`;p.querySelector('.action').textContent=step===0?'Before the escape choice.':step===1?(d.outcome.escape?'Uses the requested teleport; recorded position shown above.':'Requests no escape.'):(d.outcome.cast?`The scheduled native spell executes; this recording loses ${d.outcome.hp_lost} HP.`:'No spell is scheduled: the caster no longer has a terrain-clear path or range.');document.getElementById(panel+'-log').textContent=d.raw}let a=c.before.outcome,b=c[variant.value].outcome;document.getElementById('outcome').textContent=select.value==='blocked'&&variant.value!=='path-only'?'Still-hit counterexample: spends one scroll and still loses 54 HP, versus 59 HP with no scroll originally.':select.value==='blocked'&&variant.value==='path-only'?'Path correction alone does not fix the mixed-attack error: still stays and loses 59 HP.':select.value==='boulder-control'&&variant.value!=='after'?'Separate path diagnostic changes this control: spends 2 mana and loses 29 HP versus 18 HP originally; this is not uniform safety.':a.hp_after===b.hp_after&&a.scrolls_spent===b.scrolls_spent&&a.mana_spent===b.mana_spent?'Unchanged primary control: same choice, resources and native damage.':`Recorded final health: ${a.hp_after} → ${b.hp_after} HP. Resource costs remain visible above.`;for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-step]'))b.classList.toggle('active',Number(b.dataset.step)===step)}select.addEventListener('change',()=>{step=2;draw()});variant.addEventListener('change',draw);for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-step]'))b.addEventListener('click',()=>{step=Number(b.dataset.step);draw()});draw();</script></html>'''
(root/'replay.html').write_text(html.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(data).replace('<','\\u003c')))
(root/'replay-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2)+'\n')
print('Open in your browser:',root/'replay.html')
